template:
DISPATCH TO: {agent}
MODE: review
INTENT KD: {intent_kd}
SESSION DATE: {session_date}
SESSION ID: {session_id}
GENERATION: {generation}
SCOPE: {scope}
RESULT KD: {result_kd}
KD PATHS: {kd_paths}

---

Load the kd-system skill. Read the INTENT KD at {intent_kd}. Read SPEC KDs, PLAN KDs, and IMPL KDs from KD PATHS. Review the implementation AND run the security audit per the scope above. Produce a REVIEW KD (review findings + audit section) at {result_kd} using the naming convention: knowledge/review-<name>-<session_id>-gen{generation}.md

Verdict Rules (binding):
- Write the verdict into the review KD frontmatter as a single `verdict: PASS | FAIL | FUNDAMENTAL` field — it is the machine source protocol-gate reads at VERIFY.
- `MISSING` (absent or invalid verdict) blocks VERIFY — never treated as PASS.
- `PASS` advances only when the review KD is newer than the newest impl KD (fresh PASS after the last fix); a stale PASS blocks.
- `FAIL` regresses VERIFY→SWARM and reopens exactly the milestone row(s) the FAIL findings cite.
- CITATION MANDATE: every FAIL finding MUST cite at least one milestone token (M\d+ or impl-<id>-). A FAIL verdict with zero milestone citations is MALFORMED — it blocks, regresses nothing, and reopens nothing; re-dispatch the review with proper citations.
